  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates two models for cross-sectional stock return prediction on TOPIX500: quantum circuit learning (QCL) and a tensor network (MPS) model, against linear regression and neural networks. QCL uses 10 qubits, depth 3, and 90 parameters in noiseless Qulacs simulation, achieving ER 1.35%, TE 6.18%, and IR 0.22; the best classical baseline NN2 reaches ER 1.76% and IR 0.41, while the tensor network achieves the best overall backtest with ER 3.71% and IR 0.69.",
